.TH CHMAP_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chmap_remove \- remove a key-value pair (type-inferred)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

ccol_retval_t chmap_remove(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for chmap_delete_elem() that returns the result code
and does not stop the program for key_not_found.

The lookup key goes through the DECLARED key type of the map, in the
same way as in chmap_insert(3), so a key that the map stored through
that conversion is only ever found again by a lookup that makes the
same conversion. Both a literal and a computed expression are accepted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  Hash map to remove from
key      Key to remove
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns ccol_success when the macro removes the key
Returns ccol_key_not_found when the map does not hold the key
Returns ccol_invalid_args when key is a NULL character pointer, which
is not a string
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Does not stop the program for key_not_found
Frees the memory of the key and of the value
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
int key = 42;
ccol_retval_t r = chmap_remove(map, key);
if (r == ccol_key_not_found) {
  printf("Key not found\en");
}
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_delete_elem (3),
.BR chmap_insert (3)
